WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.020
- Well y'all know how we
end things around here.

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:03.960
I find something fun and uplifting online,

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:04.890
and I share it with you

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.189
this is what I'm liking.

00:00:06.189 --> 00:00:07.543
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.543 --> 00:00:08.850
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:10.780
So, so often on this show,

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.290
we talk about the chain
reaction of kindness

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:15.520
and that's exactly what
two Michigan teachers

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.960
want to prove to their
elementary students.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.140
So they ask the kids
to collect cereal boxes

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:22.300
to donate to the local food bank,

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.880
but before they delivered the cereal,

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.590
the teachers assembled the boxes

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:28.540
and aligned down multiple
hallways in the school

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:29.850
and with the kids watching,

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:32.750
they demonstrated how
compassion really can

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.202
create a domino effect, check this out.

00:00:35.202 --> 00:00:38.895
- Three, two, one.
- [Kids] Three, two, one.

00:00:38.895 --> 00:00:41.562
(all cheering)

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:49.567
- I love that.
(audience clapping)

00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:52.153
I'm like 40 and I find so
much amusement from that.

00:00:52.153 --> 00:00:55.150
We have the teachers behind
the cereal domino run

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:56.130
on the line right now.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:59.335
Let's say hi to Crystal and Angela y'all.

00:00:59.335 --> 00:01:00.168
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:01:00.168 --> 00:01:01.001
What's up ladies?

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:03.190
Oh my God, love that!

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:04.440
I love that y'all did that.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:05.670
I'm literally 40 years old

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:08.300
and I like get so much joy from that.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.000
So tell us more about this project though

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.610
and how many boxes we're
in your domino chain?

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:14.710
- Yeah, so our mission
here at South Elementary

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:16.030
is joyful learning

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:18.160
and so this is a way that we lived it

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:21.040
and it's just summed up into
those two quick little words.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.870
- Cereal's actually the
number one requested food item

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:24.770
by food banks,

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:28.400
because we can tailor that
more towards what kids want.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.600
Last year, we were able to
raise 711 boxes of cereal

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:34.940
and we thought that was pretty amazing.

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:36.520
This year, we were able to raise

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:38.962
1094 boxes of cereal.

00:01:38.962 --> 00:01:39.963
- Oh my gosh!

00:01:39.963 --> 00:01:42.410
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:43.580
- Last year I had three students

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:44.810
and this year I had two students

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:47.750
that benefited from the
donated boxes of cereal.

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:49.810
So as teachers, we know
how important this is

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:52.320
and how the need is very, very real.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.070
- It's so cool that
you're teaching them that

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:55.030
at a young age too.

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:56.130
It's so important 'cause when they learn

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:57.530
that kind of kindness and compassion

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:58.780
and empathy at such a young age

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:00.410
it carries out into
their adulthood, right?

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:01.910
So thank y'all for doing that

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:04.330
and also for making it fun

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:06.530
because what did it take
to set up all those boxes?

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:07.890
How long did that take?

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:09.820
- It actually took us about 40 minutes

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:12.730
all hands on deck throughout the district.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:15.700
We had people running boxes to us,

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:17.670
they were handing boxes off

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:21.040
as we assembled and engineered
the entire run itself.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.790
I was jumping over the boxes,

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:25.080
making Angela really nervous

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.660
but I assured her that I had under control

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:30.461
every 10th box or so we removed a box

00:02:30.461 --> 00:02:32.500
so that way if 10 of 'em fell

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:34.450
it really wasn't that big of a deal.

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:36.200
- Oh see, that's a teacher move.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.020
That's a teacher move right there.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:39.330
Yeah 'cause I would not
have thought of that

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.510
I was like, oh my God, one
kid, one kid knocks it over

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:42.810
and the whole thing you
have to start over again.

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:44.430
I was like, yeah.
(audience laughing)

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.620
- So once all the boxes were lined up,

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:47.770
we had the kids go out in the hall

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:49.230
and we'd tell 'em it was like lava

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:50.630
so they couldn't touch it.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:53.880
And amazingly with 345 students

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:56.980
in a young five through
second grade classroom,

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.640
no boxes were touched,

00:02:58.640 --> 00:02:59.840
nothing was knocked over.
(kids cheering)

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:02.880
So it just shows how
responsible they really are.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.860
The run itself took about two minutes

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:06.560
and as you can hear in the video

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:09.040
the kids were just amazed and excited

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:12.620
and it just really shows
what impact that we have

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:13.850
and we're just really excited

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:15.710
to continue to do it in the future.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:16.655
- I love that.

00:03:16.655 --> 00:03:17.488
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:03:17.488 --> 00:03:18.880
Well, thank you so much Crystal,

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:19.840
thank you Angela.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.743
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:03:21.743 --> 00:03:22.640
(bell rings)

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:23.957
And that's not all.

00:03:23.957 --> 00:03:24.810
- [Angela And Crystal] Thank you!

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.190
- Oh absolutely that's not all though

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:28.410
our season long partner
Pilot Pin Makers of Friction,

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:30.800
the go to race will pin
of the Kelly Clarkson show

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:32.750
want to celebrate those
creating fearlessly

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:33.690
just like y'all,

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:36.820
so they're gonna give
Watervliet Public Schools

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:37.893
a thousand dollars.

00:03:37.893 --> 00:03:42.019
(all cheering and clapping)

00:03:42.019 --> 00:03:42.953
Thank you ladies.

